# Working in this repo

- Read [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) and [docs/behaviour.md](../../docs/behaviour.md) before you edit.
- Follow [How a change happens](../../AGENTS.md#how-a-change-happens).
- A pull request description follows [the change summary](../../.github/pull_request_template.md). Section headings are 📝 What changes, ⚙️ How it works, 🔍 How to review, and ✅ Checks. Emojis are only for those headings. Issue titles and pull request titles stay plain sentences. How to review stays concise: name the script or file to run, in backticks, give two or three ready-to-paste commands that show the expected result (single quotes around $ amounts), and one sentence on what each command should return. Leave How to review out when there's nothing to try by hand.
- Stay inside the current issue.
- Every change to how the assistant behaves must match [docs/behaviour.md](../../docs/behaviour.md).
- Never change anything in [docs/agreements.md](../../docs/agreements.md), and never weaken a test to make it pass. Ask the client first.
